Finding a good web designer in Merthyr Tydfil is harder than it sounds. There's no shortage of people willing to build you a website — but finding someone who understands your local market, builds sites that generate enquiries, and supports you properly after launch is a different matter.

Here's how to make the right choice for your Merthyr business.

## Get clear on what you need first

Before you speak to anyone, be clear about the outcome you're looking for. Do you need to generate more phone enquiries? Rank on Google for local searches? Look more professional to potential clients? Sell something online?

A good web designer asks about your business and goals before talking about design or price. One who jumps straight to platforms and timelines without asking about your business is prioritising their process over your results.

## Look at their portfolio critically

Every designer has a portfolio. What matters is whether those websites actually work — not whether they look good in a screenshot.

When you're reviewing someone's portfolio, ask:

- Do those sites load quickly on a phone?
- Is it obvious what the visitor is supposed to do on each page?
- Do those businesses show up in local Google searches?
- Are these real clients with real businesses?

If a designer can point to a Merthyr trade business or local service that's generating enquiries from Google, that's a much stronger signal than a polished design concept for a company you've never heard of.

[View the NC Digital portfolio](/portfolio/) to see real work for South Wales businesses, including Merthyr clients.

## Ask about local SEO — specifically

Merthyr Tydfil is a smaller market than Cardiff or Swansea, but it's still competitive. Local tradespeople, service businesses, and retailers are all competing for the same Google results in CF47 and the surrounding Valleys postcodes.

Your website needs to be built with those local searches in mind — not as a generic business site that happens to mention Merthyr.

Ask any designer:

- Do you include on-page SEO as standard?
- How will you target the right Merthyr and Valleys search terms?
- Will my site be set up in Google Search Console?

At NC Digital, every [Merthyr Tydfil web design](/web-design-merthyr-tydfil/) project includes SEO foundations as standard. We're based in Merthyr — we know the local search landscape better than anyone. For ongoing growth, our [Merthyr SEO service](/seo-merthyr-tydfil/) can build on that with a dedicated monthly campaign.

## Work with someone who knows the area

There's a real difference between a designer who knows Merthyr Tydfil and one who's working from a brief and a map. Local businesses here have specific customers with specific expectations — Valleys customers, local tradespeople, businesses in Dowlais, Cyfarthfa, and the surrounding areas.

A designer who's based here or has worked extensively with Merthyr businesses will build that context into your site naturally. One who doesn't know the area will produce a website that could belong to any business anywhere.

## Watch for these red flags

- **No real portfolio** — if they can't show you live examples, walk away
- **Vague pricing with no clear scope** — you deserve a quote before you commit
- **No talk of SEO or local visibility** — any good designer raises this early
- **Templates sold as custom work** — ask directly whether your site will be built from scratch
- **No support plan after launch** — what happens when you need a change or something breaks?

## Ask what happens after launch

Your site needs hosting, maintenance, and support to stay fast and secure. Be clear on what's included:

- [Website hosting and security](/services/website-hosting-security/)
- [Maintenance packages](/services/website-maintenance-packages/)
- What the process is for small changes and updates

## Don't forget branding

If your logo looks dated or you don't have consistent brand colours, a new website will just display that on a better canvas. Our [logo design service in Merthyr Tydfil](/logo-design-merthyr-tydfil/) creates a complete brand identity from £200 — reduced if you're also getting a new website.

## The right choice for your Merthyr business

The right web designer for a Merthyr Tydfil business is one who understands the local market, builds for local search performance, quotes clearly, and sticks around after launch.

